invariant: INV-39
file: handshake_post.c
catches: unit
reason: ch_read rekeys on a KeyUpdate that has bytes after it in its
  record and reads on, in either role. colibri sent a server one record
  holding two KeyUpdates and got two answers, and a message that starts
  after a KeyUpdate finishes under the next key. RFC 9846 section 5.1
  makes that unexpected_message. test/session_record_end_tests.h holds
  the KeyUpdate that ends its record and the one with a byte after it.

--- old
        } else if (type == HS_KEY_UPDATE && msg_len == 1 && body[0] <= 1 &&
                   off + 4 + msg_len == n) {
--- new
        } else if (type == HS_KEY_UPDATE && msg_len == 1 && body[0] <= 1) {
